3️⃣ Now we need to receive the positions of the ponies during the race. 💡The backend exposes a
    websocket channel for this, 💡but we are going to work without it first, by emulating these
    positions using RxJS.
    👉To represent this position, add another interface called PonyWithPositionModel in pony-model.ts.
    👉This new interface will extend PonyModel and have a field position of type number. Indeed, the
    server will emit positions as integers for each pony between 0 (the pony has not started) and
    100 (the pony has completed the race), until one of the ponies reaches 100.
    pony-model.ts:

        export interface PonyModel {
            // omitted
        }
        export interface PonyWithPositionModel extends PonyModel {
            position: number;
        }

    👉Create also a LiveRaceModel interface in race-model.ts, containing a field ponies as an array
    of PonyWithPositionModel and a status field.
    👉This status field is an enum on server-side, with 3 possible values:
    -> 'PENDING' if the race is not started yet
    -> 'RUNNING' if it’s currently started
    -> 'FINISHED' if we missed the action
    👉Let’s add an optional status? field in our RaceModel, and a mandatory status field in our
    LiveRaceModel with these values.
    race-model.ts:

        export interface RaceModel {
            // omitted
            status?: 'PENDING' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED';
        }

        export interface LiveRaceModel {
            ponies: Array<PonyWithPositionModel>;
            status?: 'PENDING' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED';
        }


