5️⃣ Let’s go back to our Live component. We want to:
    👉first, fetch the race details (to get the name, the start instant, the initial status, etc…​)
    Create a required input named raceId, transformed with numberAttribute, so the router can
    bind the dynamic URL parameter to it. create a first resource field to store the result of
    RaceService.get().       
    live.ts:

        private readonly raceService = inject(RaceService);
        readonly raceId = input.required({ transform: numberAttribute });
        protected readonly initialRace = this.raceService.get(() => this.raceId());

    👉then, fetch the live information with the updated status and the positions of the ponies.
    We’ll store these information in an object described by the following interface (that you
    can add in the live.ts file):

        interface RaceModelWithPositions extends RaceModel {
            poniesWithPosition: Array<PonyWithPositionModel>;
        }
    
    (As you can see RaceModelWithPositions is the same as the RaceModel interface, but with an
    additional field poniesWithPosition, representing the ponies with their positions.)
    👉Then add a new resource, that depends on the initial race resource and call RaceService.live()
    only once the race has been loaded. You can use rxResource() for that:
    live.ts:

        protected readonly initialRace = this.raceService.get(() => this.raceId());
        private readonly liveRace = rxResource<RaceModelWithPositions, RaceModel | undefined>({
            params: () => {
                if (!this.initialRace.hasValue()) {
                    return undefined;
                }
                return this.initialRace.value();
            },
            stream: ({ params: race }) =>
                this.raceService.live(race.id).pipe(
                    map(live => ({ ...race, poniesWithPosition: live.ponies, status: live.status })),
                    startWith({ ...race, poniesWithPosition: [] })
                )
        });

    👉Add a computed() field named raceModel that returns undefined while the initial race is not
    loaded, or the value of the live resource once available:
    live.ts:

        protected readonly raceModel = computed<RaceModelWithPositions | undefined>(() => {
            if (!this.initialRace.hasValue()) {
                return undefined;
            }
            const race = this.initialRace.value();
            return this.liveRace.hasValue() ? this.liveRace.value() : { ...race, poniesWithPosition: [] };
        });



6️⃣ Then, 👉use the raceModel field in an h1 element to display the name of the race in the template.
    The last thing to do is to display our moving ponies. In the template 👉add a div with a class
    pony-wrapper, which will be repeated for each pony in the poniesWithPosition array.
    👉Inside this div, add a Pony for the current pony, with an attribute isRunning set to true
    (to make the pony run, of course. (property binding)).

    👉We now need to "move" our ponies based on their positions. To do this, set the 'margin-left'
    style property to (pony.position - 5)%, by adding [style.marginLeft.%]="pony.position - 5" to
    the div wrapping the pony.
    live.html:

        @if (raceModel(); as raceModel) {
            <h1>{{ raceModel.name }}</h1>
            @for (pony of raceModel.poniesWithPosition; track pony.id) {
                <div class="pony-wrapper" [style.marginLeft.%]="pony.position - 5" style="transition: margin-left 1s linear">
                <pr-pony [ponyModel]="pony" [isRunning]="true" />
                </div>
            }
        }


